#!/bin/zsh
# Image prompts for every plate and frame of "Don't give it back". Run from anywhere:
#   tools/frames.sh room-night|props|mirror|table|start|mirror-key|end|handover|dawn-unlit|fist
# Needs GEMINI_API_KEY. Writes into frames/ (fist into frames/dark/).
set -e
HERE=${0:A:h}
cd "$HERE/../frames"
export ASPECT=16:9
G="$HERE/../../generated/pass-4-seven-segments/tools/gen.py"
CAST="$HERE/../cast"
SC="$HERE/../frames"
LOOK="Photoreal 35mm film still, fine grain, natural textures, Dutch Golden Age painterly realism like an Adriaen van Ostade or Vermeer interior, 16:9. No text, no logo, no watermark, nothing modern."
POV="First-person POV: the camera is the eyes of a young woman sitting on a low stool at the table, seated eye height, 40mm-equivalent lens, level horizon along the far table edge, slight downward pitch. Her body, shoulders and face are NOT visible; at most her own two hands and forearms with cream linen sleeves rolled to the elbow enter from the bottom of the frame."
TABLE="The foreground is the table top: a small, low, rough oak table of three wide planks with visible gaps between them, dark and greasy with use, black burn rings, knife cuts, ink stains, white tallow drips, crumbs and a sticky grey film, corners rounded by wear. On it, in these positions: at the bottom edge nearest the viewer, a cracked earthenware bowl holding a crust of dark rye bread with crumbs around it, a horn spoon and a little pile of tallow scrapings; at the centre, a short, greasy, crooked, half-burnt tallow candle stub with thick yellowish drips in a small dented, darkened brass candlestick with a wide drip pan full of old tallow; to the right of the candle, the old rectangular hand mirror from the reference; on the left side of the table, a pincushion, spools of linen thread, iron shears, fabric scraps and a folded fine linen shirt. No matches, no tinderbox, no flint, no lamp, no second candle."
ROOM="Across the table: the cramped, poor one-room home of a seamstress, Dutch town about 1636, as in the room reference image: low soot-blackened beams, crumbling limewash walls with bare grey plaster patches and damp stains, cracked red-brown brick floor; directly across the table, in the back wall, one small window of a few dull diamond glass panes in bent lead cames with one pane of oiled paper and a warped shutter half open; background left a small cold blackened brick hearth with grey ash, no fire, an empty iron pot and an empty peat basket; background right a low bed with a straw mattress and patched grey blanket; a string line with patched shirts under the beams. Directly across the table, right under the window, a low old chair with a frayed broken rush seat, a sagging basket and a heap of finer customers' clothes beside it."
MOTHER="In that chair, facing the camera across the table: the Mother from the reference portrait, exactly the same face, white linen coif hiding all her hair, charcoal-black wool jacket, faded indigo work apron with one deep front patch pocket, brown wool shawl, raw red work-worn hands with a brass thimble."
OLD="Everything is very old, poor and worn: cobwebs hang between the soot-black beams, limewash flakes off in sheets, black mould creeps in the corners, the brick floor is sunken and broken, the window panes are grimy and cracked, the table is grey with grime and grease, the bowl is chipped and stained, every cloth is threadbare, darned and faded, dust everywhere; nothing is clean, polished or new."
DARK="Very low-key night lighting like a Rembrandt night scene, about three in the morning: most of the frame is near-black; one narrow cold blue-grey shaft of moonlight from the small window falls only on the Mother's hands, the shirt she mends and half of her face; the table, its objects and the viewer's hands are barely visible, catching only faint cold rim light; walls, beams and the hearth are dim outlines. No candle, no lamp, no fire is lit anywhere."
NOSELF="Strictly first person: there is NO head, hair, face, ear, shoulder or back of the viewer anywhere in the frame, and no other person except the Mother. The frame edges show only the room and the table."
SLOOK="Photoreal 35mm film still, fine grain, natural textures, Dutch Golden Age painterly realism like a Vermeer interior, 16:9. No text, no logo, no watermark, no modern objects."
SROOM="The cramped, poor one-room home of a seamstress in a Dutch town, about 1636, like an Adriaen van Ostade cottage interior: low, soot-blackened ceiling beams very close overhead, rough walls of crumbling limewash with patches of bare grey plaster, damp yellow-brown water stains and black soot above the hearth, an uneven floor of worn, cracked old red-brown bricks with grime in the joints. Seen from the main camera position at seated eye height on the front side of the room, looking at the back wall. Exact layout from left to right: at the screen-left, a small, cold, blackened brick hearth with grey ash and no fire, no embers, an empty iron cooking pot hanging on a sooty chain, and an EMPTY wicker peat basket beside it on the floor. In the back wall, a little left of centre, one small window of a few dull diamond-shaped glass panes in bent lead cames, some panes cracked, one pane replaced with a scrap of oiled paper, a warped wooden shutter half open. In the middle of the room, about one metre in front of the back wall, a small, rough, scarred oak table, its top marked with burn rings, knife cuts and old wax drips, one leg propped up with a wedge of wood; a three-legged stool with a worn, hollowed seat stands behind it facing the camera. Right at the LEFT end of the table, within arm reach of the stool, a low old chair with a frayed, broken rush seat, and beside it on the floor a sagging wicker basket and a heap of clothes from richer customers waiting to be mended (fine linen shirts and a velvet sleeve, much better than anything else in the room). A sagging string line under the ceiling with a few patched shirts drying on it. At the screen-right, in the corner, a plain low wooden bed with a straw-filled mattress and a grey, much-patched wool blanket. On the table, exactly two objects: at the centre, a short, greasy, half-burnt tallow candle stub, crooked, with thick yellowish drips, in a small dented, darkened brass candlestick with a little green tarnish; to its right, a small rectangular hand mirror lying FACE DOWN, showing only its worn back. Everything is old, cheap, worn, mended and slightly dirty; nothing is new, polished or decorative."
SNIGHT="Deep night. The only light is cold blue-grey moonlight through the leaded window, falling in a pale patch on the brick floor in front of the chair and the table; the rest of the room is in deep blue shadow but every object is readable. The candle is unlit: a cold black wick, no flame, no glow, no smoke anywhere. The hearth is dead cold."
case $1 in
  room-night) python3 $G room-night.png "The reference image shows the mirror that lies face down on the table. $SLOOK $SROOM $SNIGHT No people in the room." mirror.png;;
  props) python3 $G props.png "$SLOOK Close-up still life on a rough, scarred oak table top marked with burn rings, knife cuts and old wax drips, at night, lit only by cold blue moonlight from the left. A short, greasy, half-burnt tallow candle stub, crooked, with thick yellowish drips, in a small dented, darkened brass socket candlestick with a little green tarnish and a wide drip pan. The candle is unlit: a black wick, no flame, no glow, no smoke. To its right, the very old palm-sized rectangular hand mirror from the reference image lying face down: only its dull, cracked, chipped tortoiseshell back in bent blackened silver mounts, bound with dark thread, is visible. No handle. Nothing else on the table." mirror.png;;
  mirror) python3 $G mirror.png "$SLOOK Reference photograph on a rough, scarred wooden table in dim window light: two views side by side of the SAME very old, worn, palm-sized rectangular hand mirror, about 12 by 9 cm, Dutch, 1630s, no handle, an heirloom used for decades in a poor home. LEFT: the front, flat old mercury-backed glass gone hazy and grey, with large dark desilvered patches and black flecks spreading from the corners and a fine crack across one corner, in a thin silver rim blackened with tarnish and dented. RIGHT: the back, dull, faded, clouded tortoiseshell with a crack across it and one small corner chipped off, held in thin, bent, blackened silver mounts, the cracked part bound with a few turns of dark thread. Not shiny, not luxurious, nothing new. Plain background, nothing else.";;
  table) python3 $G table.png "$LOOK $POV Close view down onto the table at night, lit only by cold blue moonlight from the window beyond. $TABLE The mirror lies FACE DOWN, showing only its dull cracked tortoiseshell back bound with dark thread. The candle is unlit: black wick, no flame, no glow, no smoke. No hands, no people." $SC/mirror.png $SC/props.png;;
  start) python3 $G start.png "Reference images: the FIRST is the room, the SECOND the table and its objects, the THIRD the Mother; copy each exactly. $LOOK $POV $TABLE The mirror lies FACE DOWN right of the candle, showing only its cracked tortoiseshell back; it has no handle. The candle is unlit: black wick, no flame, no glow, no smoke. $ROOM $MOTHER She mends a fine linen shirt in her lap in the moonlight, eyes down. The viewer's right hand, young and slim with a cream linen sleeve, enters from the bottom right of the frame and is held out flat, palm toward the cold candle wick, about a hand's width away, fingers tense. Exactly one hand of the viewer is visible. $OLD $DARK $NOSELF" $SC/room-night.png table.png $CAST/mother-front.png;;
  mirror-key) python3 $G mirror-key.png "The FIRST image is the exact scene through the young woman's own eyes: keep the room, the table, its objects, the darkness and the Mother exactly. The SECOND image is the old mirror. The THIRD image is the face that must appear ONLY INSIDE THE MIRROR GLASS as a reflection; that woman is not anywhere else in the picture. $LOOK Change only this: the viewer's two hands, entering from the bottom of the frame, hold up ONE old rectangular hand mirror (exactly the second image, no handle) in the centre of the frame, a little below eye level. There is exactly ONE mirror in the whole picture: the place on the table where it lay is now empty bare wood. In its hazy, flecked, cracked glass is her reflection: the face from the third image, with the same freckles, the same long dark auburn braid, the same worn cream linen shirt and rust-red laced bodice, in the same dark room; the only differences are a small steady orange flame resting on her open left palm inside the reflection and her calm quiet smile. The flame in the reflection gives the glass a soft warm glow that lights the viewer's fingers; that warm glow is the only warm light in the frame. Across the table, beyond the mirror, the Mother in her white coif has looked up toward the viewer, worried, half her face in moonlight. The candle on the table is unlit: black wick, no flame. $OLD $DARK $NOSELF" start.png $SC/mirror.png $CAST/wren-front.png;;
  end) python3 $G end.png "The reference image shows the exact room, camera position, table and objects at night: keep the camera, the room, the table and every object in the same place, but this picture is a NEW moment just after sunrise. $LOOK $POV Dawn: the small window behind the Mother glows a faint grey-gold; soft, dim morning light reaches into the room, which stays mostly in shadow. On the table: the same cracked bowl with bread, the sewing things and the same dented brass candlestick, whose greasy tallow stub now burns with one small, steady, real flame casting warm light on the table and on the Mother's face. The table right of the candle is bare wood. Across the table the Mother is asleep in her chair: eyes closed, head bowed, holding the ONE old hand mirror upright against her lap in both red hands, the glass toward her apron and only the cracked tortoiseshell back facing the viewer; it is as long as her hand. The viewer's right hand rests open on the near table edge beside the candle, not touching it. $OLD $NOSELF" start.png;;
  handover) python3 $G handover.png "The FIRST image is the exact scene at night through the young woman's own eyes: keep the camera, the room, the table, every object, the darkness and the moonlight exactly as in it. The SECOND image shows how the Mother holds the mirror in her lap and how big it is; copy that grip and that exact mirror size, but NOT its dawn light. The THIRD image is the mirror itself. $LOOK Change only this: the Mother has laid the half-mended shirt over the arm of her chair and now holds the ONE old rectangular hand mirror face down in both red work-worn hands in her lap, its cracked tortoiseshell back facing up; it is as long as her hand. She is awake and looks straight at the viewer with a soft, relieved, slightly proud expression, mouth closed. The table right of the candlestick is EMPTY bare grimy wood: there is no mirror on the table and exactly ONE mirror in the whole picture. The candle is unlit: black wick, no flame, no glow, no smoke. The viewer's right hand rests on the near table edge, entering from the bottom right; no other hand of the viewer. $OLD $DARK $NOSELF" start.png end.png $SC/mirror.png;;
  dawn-unlit) python3 $G dawn-unlit.png "The reference image is the exact frame to copy: keep the camera, the room, the table, every object, the Mother's pose, her closed eyes, the mirror in her hands and its size exactly the same. $LOOK Change only this: the candle is NOT lit. Its black wick is cold: no flame, no glow, no ember, no smoke, and no warm candlelight anywhere on the table or on the Mother's face. The only light is soft pale dawn light from the small window behind the Mother. The viewer's right hand rests on the near table edge. Exactly ONE mirror, in the Mother's hands; nothing else changes. $NOSELF" end.png;;
  fist) python3 $G dark/fist.png "The FIRST image is the exact scene at night through the young woman's own eyes: keep the camera, the room, the table, every object, the darkness and the dim window exactly as in it. The SECOND image is the old mirror. $LOOK Change only this: the ONE old rectangular hand mirror lies face down on the table to the right of the candlestick, showing only its dull cracked tortoiseshell back, the same size as in the first image. The viewer's right hand, entering from the bottom right, rests on the table just beside the mirror, clenched into a tight fist, knuckles pale. The Mother, across the table, has looked up from her sewing toward the viewer, worried, half her face in faint moonlight. The candle is unlit: black wick, no flame, no glow. The small window shows only a dark blue-black sky and lets in only a faint sliver of moonlight. $OLD $DARK $NOSELF" dark/start.png $SC/mirror.png;;
  *) echo "unknown frame: $1"; exit 1;;
esac
